:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ENDTCPSVR.End TCP/IP Server (ENDTCPSVR)
:P.Use the End TCP/IP Server (ENDTCPSVR) command to end TCP/IP servers
through the servers framework.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCPSVR/SERVER'.Server application (SERVER)
:P.The server application for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*DDM:EPK.
:PD.DDM.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TELNET, *FTP, *SMTP, *LPD, *HTTP, *SNMP,
*ROUTED, *BOOTP, *TFTP, *REXEC, *DHCP, *DNS, *POP, *NTP, *SSHD,
*HOSTSVR, *QAP, *NETSVR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCPSVR/HTTPSVR'.HTTP server (HTTPSVR)
:P.The HTTP server for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ADMIN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCPSVR/INSTANCE'.Server instance (INSTANCE)
:P.The server instance for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCPSVR/OPTION'.How to end (OPTION)
:P.The how to end for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CNTRLD:EPK.
:PD.In a controlled way&colon. running work is given time to end on its
own.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCPSVR/DELAY'.Delay for *CNTRLD (seconds) (DELAY)
:P.How many seconds a controlled end waits before the end becomes
immediate.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 86400.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRTCPSVR.Start TCP/IP Server (STRTCPSVR)
:P.Use the Start TCP/IP Server (STRTCPSVR) command to start TCP/IP
servers through the servers framework (net/servers)&colon. their jobs
start with IBM's names in their subsystems.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPSVR/SERVER'.Server application (SERVER)
:P.The server application for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*DDM:EPK.
:PD.DDM.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTOSTART, *TELNET, *FTP, *SMTP, *LPD, *HTTP,
*SNMP, *ROUTED, *BOOTP, *TFTP, *REXEC, *DHCP, *DNS, *POP, *NTP, *SSHD,
*HOSTSVR, *QAP, *NETSVR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPSVR/RESTART'.Restart server (RESTART)
:P.The restart server for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *HTTP, *DNS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPSVR/HTTPSVR'.HTTP server (HTTPSVR)
:P.The HTTP server for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. HTTP server instance
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ADMIN.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Instance startup values
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPSVR/INSTANCE'.Server instance (INSTANCE)
:P.The server instance for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTOSTART.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
